-- PATCH_56: real payroll data for Apr-Aug 2026 (FY2026-27), imported
-- verbatim from the 3 salary sheets Yash uploaded 28 Sep 2026:
--   VFPL_Consultant_Salary_Sheet_v1.xlsx   (Apr-Jul; no Aug tab yet)
--   VFPL_Worker_Salary_Sheet_v1.xlsx        (Apr-Aug)
--   VFL_Employee_Salary_Sheet_2026_Onwards.xlsx (Apr-Aug, staff)
--
-- Column mapping verified programmatically against each sheet's own
-- header rows (row1 top-level labels + row3 sub-labels under merged
-- headers), cross-checked against known-good values already in
-- payroll_records for Aug 2026 (run-payroll's earlier backtest) before
-- trusting the extraction — e.g. VFL1064 Aug net_pay = 28400 in both
-- the sheet and the pre-existing draft row, confirming the backtest
-- was accurate and this import only needed to fill in what was missing
-- (all of Apr-Jul, plus the ~39 staff and all consultants missing from
-- the Aug draft) rather than replace anything that disagreed.
--
-- Upserts via ON CONFLICT(employee_id, month, year) so existing draft
-- rows are enriched in place, never duplicated, and marks every row
-- 'final' since this is real, already-paid HR data, not a computed
-- draft. Consultants have no basic/HRA breakup (a single flat monthly
-- fee per Master Data) so their one earnings figure is stored in
-- 'basic' for lack of a better-fitting column, given category='consultant'
-- makes this unambiguous on read. Requires PATCH_54's extra columns.
--
-- One documented judgment call: the Consultant sheet's generic 'Leave'
-- column (not broken into EL/CL/SL, unlike Worker/Staff) is stored in
-- 'el' as the closest-fit generic leave count — it is rare and small
-- (1-2 days for 2 people total across all 4 months) so this is noted
-- here rather than silently dropped.

